0 !BRICK_STATE {"schema_version":3,"status":"instruction_reconstruction_in_progress","version_label":"버전 0","reference_set":"LEGO Harry Potter Hogwarts Castle (71043)","source_manual_segments":["6590084-80.pdf","6590084-145.pdf","6607899-54.pdf","6607899-95.pdf","6607899-150.pdf","6607899-194.pdf","6607900-70.pdf","6607900-125.pdf","6607900-165.pdf","6607900-182.pdf","6607901-50.pdf","6607901-106.pdf"],"coverage":"6607901-50.pdf is booklet 22. PDF p.6–14 were reviewed as printed p.10–18 (steps 1–18). Official 64179 7x5 open-center frame and its dependencies are now in the shared assets. Steps 8–18 still have incomplete instance transforms and connectors; step14–15 local module is explicitly not root-reachable. Circular side builds on printed p.6–9 remain separate.","piece_count":25,"placement_status":"Steps 1–2 root frame and pins connected by measured 64179 hole row. part-0006 side-end transform and step5 part-0012 support bridge remain provisional. Local step14–15 rail/frame assembly exists; local step17 frame + four side pins now exists. Steps8–13,16,18 and final root transforms remain in progress.","validation":{"part_files":"shared LDraw shapes referenced","physical_fit":"Step1 pins to 64179: four hole centers/axes match at 0 LDU residual; adjacent 20-LDU layers are traversed by 2780 pins. part-0006 end datum meets frame side at (10,20,0), but retaining connector and perpendicular hole axes need follow-up. part-0012 supports and overhang are provisional. Full assembly fit not validated.","full_manual_coverage":"in_progress","geometry_checks":"instance IDs, transforms, quantities checked locally; full validator requires catalog offer metadata not verified"},"steps":[{"pages":"10–18","steps":[1,18],"evidence":"Booklet 22, printed p.10–18 were inspected as page images: p.10 steps1–2; p.11 steps3–5; p.12 steps6–7; p.13 steps8 and subassembly steps1–3; p.14 step9; p.15 steps10–11; p.16 steps12–13; p.17 steps14–15; p.18 steps16–18. The square frame shown from p.13 onward is a 5x7 Technic frame; no corresponding part DAT is in assets/parts. The thumbnails also show long beams, connectors and pins; exact frame joins constrain their placement. Exact 64179.dat later obtained from official LDraw library and verified as 7x5 open-center frame; step2 frame now geometrically connected to the four pins. Exact 64179.dat obtained from official LDraw library and verified as the 7x5 open-center frame; step2 frame now geometrically joined to the four pins.","placement":"part-0006 at [0,20,0], identity: 32278 local/global hole array axis Z; holes axis +Y. part-0001 32524 is at [0,0,0], identity; its pins sit at z=-60,-20,20,60 with X→+Y. Their lines coincide and pin span crosses the 20-LDU layer interface. Existing parts 7–24 remain provisional. Steps8–18 geometry pending accurate frame asset and item mapping. Added 64179 at [-40,20,0], identity. Its local Y-axis hole centers [40,0,z], z=-60,-20,20,60, transform to [0,20,z], sharing the 4 pin axes and spanning the adjoining layer. Added 64179 at [-40,20,0], identity; local hole centers [40,0,z], z=-60,-20,20,60 transform to [0,20,z], matching the four pin axes and adjoining layer. Added the 64179 frame at [-40,20,0]; four step1 pins align with its through-holes. Recomputed step2 part-0006 beam endpoint to [10,20,0] using 32278 local hole z=-140 mapped to +X; the retaining connector remains provisional."},{"pages":"17","steps":[14],"evidence":"Booklet 22 printed p.17 step14 callout and build diagram show one yellow 7-hole Technic beam with four friction pins as a standalone subassembly. This is independent of unresolved frame placement.","placement":"Created internal submodel hogwarts-step14.ldr in local coordinates: 32524 centered, four 2780 pins at beam holes z=-60,-20,20,60, y=10, local X→+Y. This local build is not yet root-reachable or counted as placed; its global transform is deferred to the step15–18 frame contacts."},{"pages":"17","steps":[14,15],"evidence":"Printed p.17 step14 yellow 32524 with four pins; step15 adds a 64179 7x5 Technic frame and a 32278 long beam.","placement":"Extended hogwarts-step14.ldr locally with 64179 at [-40,20,0], aligning its four Y-axis holes to step14 pins. Added 32278 at [150,20,0], Ry(90), placing its first hole/end datum at frame side [10,20,0]. This local assembly is unplaced; frame/rail locking remains pending steps16–18."},{"pages":"18","steps":[17],"evidence":"Printed p.18 step17 callout shows one 64179 7x5 frame and four 2780 pins. The DAT side-hole row at x=50,z=-60,-20,20,60 has +X axes.","placement":"Built a local unplaced submodel hogwarts-step17.ldr. Pins use identity rotation (2780 local X→frame side +X), centered at the frame outer-face plane x=50 and each called-out side-hole z position. Four hole-axis line residuals are zero; global tie to the step14–16 assembly is pending."}],"instances":[{"id":"part-0001","group":"frame","part":"32524.dat","gobricks_id":"","sku":"","color":14,"position":[0,0,0],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"shape_verified_sale_unmapped","placement_note":"Step 1 yellow Technic 7-hole beam; local origin centered; official 32524.dat has hole centers every 20 LDU along local Z and through-hole axes +Y. Manual orientation follows the horizontal callout."},{"id":"part-0002","group":"frame","part":"2780.dat","gobricks_id":"","sku":"","color":0,"position":[0,10,-60],"matrix":[0,-1,0,1,0,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"shape_verified_sale_unmapped","placement_note":"Step 1 pin at selected beam hole z=-60; beam hole axis R*(0,1,0)=(0,1,0); pin local X rotated to +Y. Origin at upper beam face y=10; nominal insertion span y=-8..10 (18 LDU) into 20-LDU beam thickness, leaving 2 LDU to far face; axial line and depth are separate checks."},{"id":"part-0003","group":"frame","part":"2780.dat","gobricks_id":"","sku":"","color":0,"position":[0,10,-20],"matrix":[0,-1,0,1,0,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"shape_verified_sale_unmapped","placement_note":"Step 1 pin at sele